      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    market_index_values = [3, 2, 4, 5, 6]\n    nav_changes = [5, 4, 6, 7, 9]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    mean_index = sum(market_index_values) / len(market_index_values)\n    mean_nav = sum(nav_changes) / len(nav_changes)\n\n    numerator = sum(\n        (x - mean_index) * (y - mean_nav)\n        for x, y in zip(market_index_values, nav_changes)\n    )\n    denominator = sum((x - mean_index) ** 2 for x in market_index_values)\n    slope = numerator / denominator\n\n    # return answer\n    return round(slope, 2)\n```",
